    "industrial_process_notes": "First synthesized in the early 1930s by Wallace Carothers' research group at DuPont's Experimental Station. Commercial interest surged during the 1970s-1980s polymer boom, declined through the 1990s, then resurged in the 1990s-2000s with tissue engineering and 3D printing applications. Made via ring-opening polymerization of epsilon-caprolactone using stannous octoate catalyst; low-molecular-weight alcohols regulate final molecular weight.",
    "synthesis_scheme_image": null
  },
